  "runner_up_case": "The strongest honest case for FALSE rests on three weaknesses in the record rather than on positive contrary proof. First, no primary source was ever retrieved: court_records came back empty on every query (partly explicable because CourtListener does not index Austrian courts), the Reuters article fetch failed and its Wayback lookup was empty, so the key Reuters quote ('increasing his prison sentence to 30 months from the original two years') exists only as a search snippet. Second, the single contrary item, bluewin.ch (2026-02-17), states that in October 2025 Benko was 'not finally sentenced to two years' imprisonment in Innsbruck' in the first fraudulent-krida proceedings; if the full article shows the October verdict was not a sentencing order at all — conviction with sentencing deferred, a partly conditional term, or a verdict annulled before taking effect — the claim as stated would be materially wrong. Third, there is a real conflation risk between two near-identical proceedings: the October 2025 case (€300,000 payment to his mother) and the September 2026 retrial of the €360,000 rent/operating-costs case, which ended in a 30-month sentence; an analyst could have attached the wrong figure to the wrong trial. The truncated ORF snippet ('teilweise schuldig gesprochen und zu…') also leaves open that the October sentence was partially conditional. That said, this case is thin: 'not finally sentenced' most naturally means 'sentenced but not final (appeal pending)', which qualifies rather than refutes the claim, and contemporaneous reports (The Local 2025-10-15, CoStar 2025-10-17) plus five independent September 2026 retrospectives (Reuters, Spiegel, Die Presse, ORF Tirol, Krone) all describe an unconditional two-year first-instance sentence by the Landesgericht Innsbruck in October 2025. FALSE is therefore the runner-up, not the leader.",
  "would_flip_it": [
    "Full text of the bluewin.ch 2026-02-17 article showing the October 2025 Innsbruck verdict was not a sentencing order at all (sentencing deferred, verdict suspended or annulled before taking effect) rather than merely not yet final pending appeal.",
    "An APA wire item, ORF report or court document stating the October 2025 sentence was conditional in part or of a different length (e.g. 'teilweise bedingt' or 18 months), contradicting the unconditional two-year term reported by Krone and ORF.",
    "A credible correction or retraction from The Local, CoStar or APA indicating the contemporaneous October 2025 'two years in prison' reports were erroneous.",
    "Evidence that the October 2025 proceeding ended in acquittal on the sentenced count, or that the person sentenced was a namesake and not the Signa founder René Benko."
  ]
